o coverage and buys no round.", "about": {"review_id": "rev-20261110T000725Z-74106453", "fid": "R-1"}, "oid": "O-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "Search's deprecated flag now changes for some types, with no live check and a changelog verb that overstates add", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. The R-7 fix is sound (one IsDeprecated helper, all three sites pass through it; a search for 'Obsolete' in ComponentRegistry.cs finds no second rule). Two record gaps ride with it, both in non-judgeable files, so both are free and belong in the same commit. (1) ComponentRegistry is host-coupled and cannot be unit-tested, and VRF-018 has no item for search; add one, e.g. gh_canvas(action='search', query='Rectangle') and 'C# Script' report deprecated=true for the old GUIDs the evidence note already names (0ca0a214-..., a9a8ebd2-..., 3e5582a1-...), which v1.5.0 may report as current. (2) The new CHANGELOG entry says add 'then refused as deprecated'; add does not refuse a deprecated type, it passes over it when a current twin exists and uses it with a warning when it is the only match. Say 'treated as deprecated'. Default disposition is accept; neither changes code.", "about": {"review_id": "rev-20261110T000725Z-74106453", "fid": "R-7"}, "oid": "O-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "title": "Python pin kept as documented behaviour; the Stream Filter pin was found inert and is still advertised as a pin", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. R-2 is resolved by the third remedy it offered: the mapping is kept, and help, server instructions, CHANGELOG, the Pinned doc comment and VRF-018 item 5 now all say that 'Python 3 Script' creates the unified Script component, with the fixture naming that GUID 'Script' as an install does. Two things for the owner rather than for another commit. (1) Keeping an exact installed name ('Python 3 Script') pointed at a differently named type is the one place the strict rule still acts on something other than the name given; it is recorded in help, changelog and a code comment but not in the change record's Decisions, so list it with the kept spellings in the PR body. (2) The same check found Stream Filter's pinned GUID (fb97f83d-...) is not installed, so that pin never applies and the name resolves by the ordinary rule; the add tip still says 'Stream Filter' always means the built-in type, which holds only while no plugin ships one of that name. Accept: fixing the tip touches GhCanvasTool.cs and buys a round for a case no install is known to hit.", "about": {"review_id": "rev-20261110T000725Z-74106453", "fid": "R-2"}, "oid": "O-3"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "title": "'rect' is said to have always meant the parameter; the tree shows that only for 'circ' and 'ln'", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. The alias fix is by construction and verified (targets Params/Rectangle, Params/Circle, Params/Line resolve through SplitQualified; EveryAliasAndPin_ResolvesToExactlyOneType iterates every alias against a catalog with the component/parameter twins, and StockCatalog_HasTheComponentParameterTwins guards the fixture). One claim in it is not supported by history: the pre-branch registry special-cased 'circle' and 'line' as parameters, but 'rect' -> 'Rectangle' had no special case and took the first exact name match in proxy order, so which type it created depended on the install. Choosing the parameter for 'rect' is the owner decision R-3 named; name it as a choice in the PR's kept-spellings list. Accept: no code edit is wanted, and rewording the comment would buy a round.", "about": {"review_id": "rev-20261110T000725Z-74106453", "fid": "R-3"}, "oid": "O-4"}], "duration_seconds": 660, "scope": "strict-inputs", "scope_chosen_by": "binding", "scope_unresolved_cause": null, "scope_reason": null, "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": ["01", "02", "03"], "chunks_proposed": ["01", "02", "03"], "chunk": "01", "base_reviewed": null, "record_lint": {"records": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-strict-inputs